# Knowledge Vault kv-v0 Schema

This active Schema Meta object is the canonical kv-v0 contract for this vault.
It is materialized from the public distribution during bootstrap. The Markdown/YAML
contract is canonical; validator code is an implementation of it, not a replacement.

## Normative contract

All knowledge-bearing Markdown objects have exactly the universal core fields `schema`,
`id`, `title`, `kind`, `state`, `scope`, `created`, and `provenance`. Kinds, lifecycle
states, metadata applicability, references, authority, evidence, body requirements, and
integrity invariants follow the accepted Knowledge Vault V0 Canonical Specification.
The implementation rule catalog is traceability only and does not independently define kv-v0.

